From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 20:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] venus: name the modifier a refused vkCreateImage asked for
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

bd remora-e5x.25 asked for exactly this and it is what finally identified
the bug. The e5x.21 failure log prints tiling, but tiling only ever says
DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT — the modifier itself lives in the pNext chain,
and the modifier is the thing the allocator has to stop handing out.

Both spellings appear and both matter: a LIST when the guest lets the
driver choose, an EXPLICIT one when it is importing a buffer that already
exists. Super Mario Run's swapchain turned out to be the explicit case:

  vkCreateImage FAILED ret=-11 format=37 extent=1055x1992
                tiling=1000158000 usage=0x97 modifier=explicit: 0x0 planes=1

ret=-11 is FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED, format 37 is R8G8B8A8_UNORM, usage 0x97
is TRANSFER_SRC|TRANSFER_DST|SAMPLED|COLOR_ATTACHMENT|INPUT_ATTACHMENT
and modifier 0x0 is DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR. NVIDIA will not create a
RENDERABLE linear-modifier image, so every frame of that app's swapchain
is refused and the app renders black while staying alive.

Diagnostic only — no behaviour change.
---
diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_image.c b/src/venus/vkr_image.c
index f4b2212e..86013a0d 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_image.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_image.c
@@ -47,10 +47,33 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkCreateImage(struct vn_dispatch_context *dispatch,
    if (!_img && args->pCreateInfo) {
       /* remora-e5x.21: a pipelined create failure surfaces later as a fatal
        * missing-object CS error — record what the driver refused. */
-      vkr_log("vkCreateImage FAILED ret=%d format=%d extent=%ux%u tiling=%d usage=0x%x",
+      /* remora-e5x.25: the refusal is useless without the MODIFIER. tiling alone
+       * only says DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT; which modifier the guest asked for is
+       * in the pNext chain, and that is the thing the allocator has to stop
+       * advertising. Both spellings appear: a LIST when the guest lets the driver
+       * choose, an EXPLICIT one when it is importing a buffer that already exists. */
+      char mods[192];
+      int n = snprintf(mods, sizeof mods, "none");
+      for (const VkBaseInStructure *p = args->pCreateInfo->pNext; p; p = p->pNext) {
+         if (p->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_LIST_CREATE_INFO_EXT) {
+            const VkImageDrmFormatModifierListCreateInfoEXT *l = (const void *)p;
+            n = snprintf(mods, sizeof mods, "list[%u]:", l->drmFormatModifierCount);
+            for (uint32_t i = 0; i < l->drmFormatModifierCount && n > 0 && n < (int)sizeof mods; i++)
+               n += snprintf(mods + n, sizeof mods - n, " 0x%llx",
+                             (unsigned long long)l->pDrmFormatModifiers[i]);
+            break;
+         }
+         if (p->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXPLICIT_CREATE_INFO_EXT) {
+            const VkImageDrmFormatModifierExplicitCreateInfoEXT *e = (const void *)p;
+            snprintf(mods, sizeof mods, "explicit: 0x%llx planes=%u",
+                     (unsigned long long)e->drmFormatModifier, e->drmFormatModifierPlaneCount);
+            break;
+         }
+      }
+      vkr_log("vkCreateImage FAILED ret=%d format=%d extent=%ux%u tiling=%d usage=0x%x modifier=%s",
               args->ret, args->pCreateInfo->format, args->pCreateInfo->extent.width,
               args->pCreateInfo->extent.height, args->pCreateInfo->tiling,
-              args->pCreateInfo->usage);
+              args->pCreateInfo->usage, mods);
    }
 }
 
